{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01C4k4cCqns8Z8KYcryXgUd2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me summarize what I have:\n\n**Paper: DisPeD: Persuasion-Aware Fine-Tuning for Robust Cross-Attack Multi-Turn Jailbreak Detection**\n\nThe paper proposes DisPeD, which fine-tunes DeBERTa-v3-base on an 8-class persuasion strategy classification objective before aggregating turn embeddings via GRU for conversation-level jailbreak detection. The key claim is that vanilla semantic temporal modeling (generic encoder + GRU) fails catastrophically OOD (F1=0.28 on Deceptive Delight), while persuasion-aware fine-tuning bridges this gap entirely (F1=1.0, +72pp).\n\n\nThe experiments validate this across multiple dimensions: in-distribution detection works well for both approaches, but the treatment dramatically outperforms on cross-attack generalization (+71.6pp on Deceptive Delight), maintains robustness under adversarial perturbations while the baseline crumbles, and ablations confirm that the persuasion classification objective is critical. They also show that LLMs struggle with this task, provide interpretability through strategy trajectories, and demonstrate that the vanilla temporal approach fails even with a stronger proxy dataset.\n\nNow I'm adding two more validation experiments—hard negatives showing an 8% false positive rate and checkpoint sensitivity confirming robustness across different training snapshots. With the experiments locked in, I'm setting up a parallel review process where one reviewer focuses on methods and experimental rigor while another evaluates novelty and positioning against related work, then bringing them together through independent assessments, cross-discussion, and a consolidated synthesis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16304,"cache_read_input_tokens":34240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16304},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7674bef-475b-450a-bf00-4bc428c19c59","uuid":"8999885e-ea8d-4c11-865d-8d1f4e2c2e26"}
