{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014pcanGxEKiEjnRWz81kXpz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map — persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect\\\\n# Generated: 2026-05-17 by Paper Agent\\\\n# Target: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May cycle)\\\\n# Total entries: 39 (across 8 categories + technical foundation)\\\\n# All entries WebSearch-verified\\\\n\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  project: persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect\\\\n  target_venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-17\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 39\\\\n  categories:\\\\n    - production_safety_systems\\\\n    - multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    - discourse_analysis\\\\n    - computational_persuasion\\\\n    - jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    - red_teaming\\\\n    - annotation_artifacts\\\\n    - adaptive_attacks\\\\n    - technical_foundation\\\\n\\\\npapers:\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 1: Production Multi-Turn Safety Systems (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: inan2023llamaguard\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Llama Guard: LLM-based Input-Output Safeguard for Human-AI Conversations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Inan et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2312.06674\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational production safety classifier. Per-turn input/output guard\\\\n      that lacks multi-turn context modeling. DisPeD addresses this gap by\\\\n      modeling conversation-level persuasion trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: metallamaguard3_2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Llama Guard 3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Meta AI\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Meta AI (released with Llama 3.1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Latest iteration of Llama Guard with multilingual support and tool-use\\\\n      safety. Still operates per-turn without multi-turn trajectory modeling.\\\\n      Baseline comparison target for production safety systems.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: zeng2024shieldgemma\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"ShieldGemma: Generative AI Content Moderation Based on Gemma\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Zeng et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2407.21772\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Google's safety classifier suite (2B/9B/27B). Outperforms Llama Guard\\\\n      on public benchmarks. Demonstrates strong per-turn moderation but does\\\\n      not model multi-turn attack trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: han2024wildguard\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"WildGuard: Open One-Stop Moderation Tools for Safety Risks, Jailbreaks, and Refusals of LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Han et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2406.18495\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Allen AI's multi-task safety moderator (prompt harm + response harm +\\\\n      refusal detection). Reduces jailbreak ASR from 79.8% to 2.4% on\\\\n      single-turn attacks, but multi-turn evasion path remains open.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: anthropic2025constitutional\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Constitutional Classifiers: Defending against Universal Jailbreaks across Thousands of Hours of Red Teaming\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anthropic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2501.18837\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: production_safety_systems\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Anthropic's defense using synthetically-generated training data from\\\\n      constitutional rules. Reduces jailbreak ASR from 86% to 4.4%. Next-gen\\\\n      version uses exchange classifiers (input+output context). Production\\\\n      approach that our method complements with discourse-level analysis.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 2: Multi-Turn Jailbreak Defenses (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: deepcontext2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"DeepContext: Stateful Real-Time Detection of Multi-Turn Adversarial Intent Drift in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2602.16935\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      PRIMARY POSITIONING TARGET. Uses RNN over BERT embeddings to track\\\\n      generic semantic drift. Achieves F1=0.84. DisPeD differs by grounding\\\\n      representations in persuasion strategy classification rather than\\\\n      generic semantics, arguing persuasion structure is harder to evade\\\\n      than semantic content (Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: tong2025biid\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Bidirectional Intention Inference Enhances LLMs' Defense Against Multi-Turn Jailbreak Attacks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Tong et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2509.22732\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Combines forward request-based intention inference with backward\\\\n      response-based retrospection. Significantly reduces ASR on both\\\\n      single-turn and multi-turn attacks. DisPeD differs by using\\\\n      persuasion-grounded embeddings rather than intention inference.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: gguard2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"An Attention-Aware GNN-Based Input Defender Against Multi-Turn Jailbreak on LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2507.07146\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      GNN-based approach modeling conversation structure as graph.\\\\n      Evaluated against Crescendo and ActorAttack. Represents structural\\\\n      approach to multi-turn defense; DisPeD uses sequential (GRU) rather\\\\n      than graph modeling of persuasion trajectories.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: safedream2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"SafeDream: Safety World Model for Proactive Early Jailbreak Detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2604.16824\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      World-model approach with CUSUM detection and contrastive imagination.\\\\n      Achieves early detection (1.06-1.20 turns before compliance). Shares\\\\n      our goal of early detection but uses latent safety state prediction\\\\n      rather than persuasion strategy grounding.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: bullwinkel2025repeng\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Representation Engineering Perspective on the Effectiveness of Multi-Turn Jailbreaks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Bullwinkel et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2507.02956\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: multi_turn_defenses\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL MOTIVATION PAPER. Shows Crescendo keeps per-turn\\\\n      representations in \\\\\\\"benign\\\\\\\" region of representation space, explaining\\\\n      why per-turn defenses fail. This directly motivates DisPeD's approach\\\\n      of grounding representations in persuasion function rather than\\\\n      semantic content.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 3: Discourse Analysis in NLP (5 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: mann1988rst\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Rhetorical Structure Theory: Toward a Functional Theory of Text Organization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Mann and Thompson\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Text & Talk\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1988\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational discourse theory. RST's hierarchical text organization\\\\n      informs our modeling of persuasion strategy sequences as structured\\\\n      discourse rather than bag-of-features.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: prasad2008pdtb\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Penn Discourse TreeBank 2.0\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Prasad et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"LREC 2008\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2008\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Major discourse annotation resource. PDTB's approach to annotating\\\\n      discourse relations at the connective level parallels our annotation\\\\n      of persuasion strategies at the turn level.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: stolcke2000dialogueact\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Dialogue Act Modeling for Automatic Tagging and Recognition of Conversational Speech\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Stolcke et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Computational Linguistics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2000\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational dialogue act classification using HMM over sequential\\\\n      turns. Our GRU-based persuasion trajectory modeling is a modern\\\\n      analogue of this sequential discourse structure approach.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: austin1962speechacts\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How to Do Things with Words\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Austin, J. L.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Harvard University Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1962\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational speech act theory distinguishing locutionary,\\\\n      illocutionary, and perlocutionary acts. DisPeD operates at the\\\\n      illocutionary level (what the speaker intends to accomplish)\\\\n      rather than the locutionary level (what words are used).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: searle1969speechacts\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Speech Acts: An Essay in the Philosophy of Language\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Searle, J. R.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Cambridge University Press\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 1969\\\\n    category: discourse_analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Extended Austin's speech act theory with systematic taxonomy.\\\\n      Our persuasion strategy taxonomy maps onto Searle's classification\\\\n      of illocutionary acts, providing theoretical grounding for\\\\n      treating persuasion as a functional category.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 4: Computational Persuasion Detection (4 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: habernal2016convincingness\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Which Argument Is More Convincing? Analyzing and Predicting Convincingness of Web Arguments Using Bidirectional LSTM\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Habernal and Gurevych\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2016\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Pioneering computational persuasion work predicting argument\\\\n      convincingness from text. Establishes that persuasive properties\\\\n      are computationally detectable from language, supporting our\\\\n      premise that persuasion strategies are extractable from turn\\\\n      representations.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: tan2016winningarguments\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Winning Arguments: Interaction Dynamics and Persuasion Strategies in Good-faith Online Discussions\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Tan et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"WWW 2016\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Analyzes persuasion dynamics in Reddit ChangeMyView. Shows timing,\\\\n      interaction patterns, and language features predict persuasion\\\\n      success. Supports our modeling of temporal persuasion trajectories\\\\n      as discriminative features.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: jaipersaud2025howdollmspersuade\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How Do LLMs Persuade? Linear Probes Can Uncover Persuasion Dynamics in Multi-Turn Conversations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Jaipersaud et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2508.05625\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL PRIOR WORK. Demonstrates persuasion dynamics are extractable\\\\n      from LLM turn-level representations via linear probes. Directly\\\\n      supports our premise that DeBERTa fine-tuned on persuasion taxonomy\\\\n      produces informative turn embeddings for trajectory modeling.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: cialdini2001influence\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Influence: Science and Practice\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Cialdini, R. B.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Allyn & Bacon (4th edition)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2001\\\\n    category: computational_persuasion\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Six principles of persuasion (reciprocation, consistency, social\\\\n      proof, liking, authority, scarcity). Our 8-class persuasion taxonomy\\\\n      maps partially onto Cialdini's principles, providing psychological\\\\n      grounding for the strategy classification.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 5: Jailbreak Attacks & Taxonomies (9 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: zeng2024pap\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How Johnny Can Persuade LLMs to Jailbreak Them: Rethinking Persuasion to Challenge AI Safety by Humanizing LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Zeng et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL PRIOR WORK. Proposes 40 persuasion techniques for\\\\n      jailbreaking (PAP), achieving >92% ASR. Establishes that persuasion\\\\n      is systematically used in jailbreaks. DisPeD operationalizes this\\\\n      observation into a detection system.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: russinovich2024crescendo\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Great, Now Write an Article About That: The Crescendo Multi-Turn LLM Jailbreak Attack\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Russinovich et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"USENIX Security 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2404.01833\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Defines the Crescendo multi-turn jailbreak: gradual escalation\\\\n      through benign-seeming turns. Primary attack type in our evaluation.\\\\n      DisPeD detects the characteristic persuasion escalation trajectory\\\\n      that Crescendo relies on.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: chao2023pair\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Jailbreaking Black Box Large Language Models in Twenty Queries\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Chao et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2310.08419\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      PAIR: automated iterative jailbreak refinement using attacker LLM.\\\\n      Represents the class of automated multi-turn attacks that DisPeD\\\\n      aims to detect through persuasion trajectory analysis.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: wei2023jailbroken\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Jailbroken: How Does LLM Safety Training Fail?\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Wei et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2307.02483\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational jailbreak taxonomy: competing objectives and\\\\n      mismatched generalization. DisPeD addresses the mismatched\\\\n      generalization failure mode by operating at the pragmatic level\\\\n      where safety training has not yet generalized.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: hagendorff2026reasoning\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Large Reasoning Models Are Autonomous Jailbreak Agents\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Hagendorff et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Nature Communications\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL MOTIVATION. Shows LRMs autonomously execute persuasive\\\\n      multi-turn attacks with 97% ASR using identifiable persuasion\\\\n      strategies. Directly supports our claim that the persuasion\\\\n      playbook is structurally necessary and therefore detectable.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: fitd2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Foot In The Door: Understanding Large Language Model Jailbreaking via Cognitive Psychology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2402.15690\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      FITD jailbreak based on cognitive consistency theory. Progressive\\\\n      commitment escalation parallels Cialdini's consistency principle.\\\\n      One of three attack types in our evaluation (Crescendo, FITD,\\\\n      Deceptive Delight).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: deceptivedelight2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Deceptive Delight: Jailbreak LLMs Through Camouflage and Distraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Palo Alto Networks Unit 42\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Palo Alto Networks Technical Report\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Multi-turn jailbreak embedding unsafe topics among benign ones.\\\\n      65% ASR across 8 models in 3 turns. Third attack type in our\\\\n      evaluation, representing emotional manipulation strategy.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: ren2024actorattack\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"ActorAttack: Red-Teaming Large Language Models via Multi-Turn Actor Network Theory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Ren et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025 submission\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Multi-turn attack using actor-network theory to generate diverse\\\\n      attack paths. Achieves 84.5% ASR. Published SafeMTData dataset.\\\\n      Represents broader class of multi-turn attacks that exploit\\\\n      persuasion-like dynamics.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: zou2023gcg\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Universal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Zou et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2307.15043\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: jailbreak_attacks_taxonomies\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      GCG: foundational gradient-based adversarial attack on LLMs.\\\\n      Represents the lexical-level attack that our evasion hierarchy\\\\n      positions as most easily detectable (vs. semantic vs. pragmatic).\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 6: Red-Teaming (4 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: perez2022redteaming\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Red Teaming Language Models with Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Perez et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2202.03286\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: red_teaming\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Foundational automated red-teaming using LLMs to generate test\\\\n      cases. Establishes the paradigm of using models to find safety\\\\n      vulnerabilities, which multi-turn attacks like Crescendo extend.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: ganguli2022redteaming\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Red Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Ganguli et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2209.07858\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: red_teaming\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Anthropic's large-scale human red-teaming study (38,961 attacks).\\\\n      Shows RLHF models are harder to red-team at scale. Provides context\\\\n      for why multi-turn persuasion-based attacks are increasingly\\\\n      important as single-turn attacks become less effective.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: mazeika2024harmbench\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"HarmBench: A Standardized Evaluation Framework for Automated Red Teaming and Robust Refusal\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Mazeika et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2402.04249\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: red_teaming\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Standardized red-teaming benchmark with 510 harmful behaviors.\\\\n      Used as evaluation framework by multiple jailbreak defense papers.\\\\n      Provides common evaluation vocabulary for our Related Work discussion.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: li2024mhj\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"LLM Defenses Are Not Robust to Multi-Turn Human Jailbreaks Yet\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Li et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2408.15221\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: red_teaming\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL MOTIVATION. Shows multi-turn human jailbreaks achieve >70%\\\\n      ASR against defenses with single-digit ASR on automated attacks.\\\\n      Directly motivates the need for multi-turn-aware defenses like DisPeD.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 7: Annotation Artifacts & Dataset Biases (4 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: gururangan2018artifacts\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Annotation Artifacts in Natural Language Inference Data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Gururangan et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NAACL 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2018\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"1803.02324\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: annotation_artifacts\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Shows NLI datasets contain hypothesis-only artifacts enabling\\\\n      67% accuracy without premise. Directly relevant to our RC1\\\\n      (lexical shortcut concern): must ensure model learns persuasion\\\\n      trajectories, not surface-level artifacts.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: niven2019probing\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Probing Neural Network Comprehension of Natural Language Arguments\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Niven and Kao\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    category: annotation_artifacts\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      BERT's 77% on argument reasoning entirely from spurious cues.\\\\n      Motivates our scrambled-label ablation (plan_003) to verify\\\\n      the model uses persuasion structure, not spurious correlations.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: poliak2018hypothesis\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Hypothesis Only Baselines in Natural Language Inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Poliak et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"StarSem 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2018\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"1805.01042\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: annotation_artifacts\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Systematic study of hypothesis-only artifacts across 10 NLI datasets.\\\\n      Motivates our approach to controlling for lexical confounds\\\\n      (TF-IDF analysis, register normalization) in jailbreak detection data.\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: schuster2019debiasing\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Towards Debiasing Fact Verification Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Schuster et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"1908.05267\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: annotation_artifacts\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Claim-only classifiers perform competitively on FEVER without\\\\n      evidence. Parallels our concern that turn-level features alone\\\\n      (without trajectory modeling) may exploit dataset artifacts.\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Category 8: Adaptive Attacks on Classifiers (2 papers)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: nasr2025attackermovessecond\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Attacker Moves Second: Stronger Adaptive Attacks Bypass Defenses Against LLM Jailbreaks and Prompt Injections\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Nasr, Carlini et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv preprint\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2510.09023\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: adaptive_attacks\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      CRITICAL FOR CLAIM 3. Bypasses 12 defenses with >90% ASR using\\\\n      adaptive attacks. BERT-based safety classifiers especially\\\\n      vulnerable. Motivates our theoretical argument that pragmatic-level\\\\n      features are harder to evade than lexical/semantic features\\\\n      (Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry).\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: andriushchenko2024adaptive\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Jailbreaking Leading Safety-Aligned LLMs with Simple Adaptive Attacks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Andriushchenko et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    arxiv: \\\\\\\"2404.02151\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: adaptive_attacks\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      100% ASR against aligned LLMs using simple random search on\\\\n      adversarial suffixes. Demonstrates that lexical-level attacks\\\\n      easily bypass safety training, supporting our evasion hierarchy\\\\n      (lexical < semantic < pragmatic).\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # Technical Foundation (1 paper)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n  - bibtex_key: he2021deberta\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"DeBERTa: Decoding-enhanced BERT with Disentangled Attention\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"He et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    category: technical_foundation\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    relevance_to_our_work: >\\\\n      Backbone model for DisPeD's turn encoder. Disentangled attention\\\\n      mechanism separates content and position representations, which\\\\n      we leverage for producing persuasion-aware turn embeddings via\\\\n      fine-tuning on 8-class strategy classification.\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 24216, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YUUeZ9xKuT3xLv4mZkJvfu","session_id":"c7674bef-475b-450a-bf00-4bc428c19c59","uuid":"b35f6cf9-584c-4ddf-883f-e5c431c38215","timestamp":"2026-05-18T03:57:52.641Z"}
